  "answer": "Someone has already asked for this. Requests for automatic or dynamic tiling in the style of i3, Hyprland or Sway have been closed as duplicates of PowerToys#2694, \"Ability to tile windows automatically\". That ticket is the one to follow, so add your use case and a thumbs-up there. PowerToys has no dynamic tiling manager today. In that thread a maintainer said auto-tiling doesn't fit FancyZones' architecture and would more likely be a separate module. The tickets I read don't mention any release plan. In the meantime, FancyZones gives you manual layouts. If you want automatic tiling now, you can try a third-party Windows tiling manager such as Komorebi, GlazeWM, FancyWM or workspacer."
